    "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n\n# PR information\n\nActivation offload deduplicates saved tensors by their storage address and dtype.\nA tensor and its transpose therefore share a CPU copy even though their values\nhave different layouts. Reloading only reshapes that copy: a square transpose\nsilently uses the wrong activations in backward, while a smaller slice can fail\nto reshape.\n\nInclude the device, shape and strides in the key, and use `data_ptr()` for the\nstarting address. Identical views still share a copy. The offload schedule and\ntransfer implementation are unchanged.\n\n## Experiment results\n\n```bash\npython -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_activation_offload_views.py -v\n```\n\nAll four tests pass on one CUDA device, including actual transfer/reload and\nFP32/BF16 backward comparisons. The original code fails the view checks and\nproduces wrong gradients for both dtypes. With CUDA hidden, two tests pass and\nthe two transfer tests are skipped.\n\nA separate single-GPU FSDP2 check wraps three small linear/nonlinear blocks and\nenables the public activation-offloading helper. The original code disagrees\nwith the eager reference on the first backward; the fix matches all gradients\nand parameters across three SGD updates. This is a small correctness check,\nnot a throughput benchmark; multi-GPU FSDP and NPU were not tested.\n\nChanged-file pre-commit checks pass. The all-files run also encounters the\nexisting isort/YAPF formatting issue in `tests/megatron/test_infonce_ddp_e2e.py`\nfrom #10150, which is outside this patch.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
